  m_Name: Dilema_DadosAbertos
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Metis.Runtime::KnowledgeEntryData
  _title: Dados abertos e privacidade
  _titleEn: Open data and privacy
  _category: 1
  _unlockTrigger: 0
  _summary: "Abrir dados p\xFAblicos permite fiscalizar o governo e criar servi\xE7os
    novos. S\xF3 que trocar nomes por c\xF3digos n\xE3o basta: cruzando informa\xE7\xF5es,
    muitas vezes d\xE1 para identificar as pessoas."
  _summaryEn: 'Opening public data lets people oversee government and build new services.
    But swapping names for codes is not enough: by cross-checking information, people
    can often be identified.'
  _realWorld: "Em 2014, Nova York liberou, por pedido de acesso \xE0 informa\xE7\xE3o,
    registros de 173 milh\xF5es de corridas de t\xE1xi. Um engenheiro mostrou que
    a anonimiza\xE7\xE3o podia ser revertida em menos de duas horas."
  _realWorldEn: In 2014, New York released records of 173 million taxi trips through
    a public records request. An engineer showed the anonymization could be reversed
    in less than two hours.
  _tradeOffs: "Revisar antes de publicar custa tempo e reduz o que pode ser aberto.
    Manter tudo fechado evita o risco e impede a fiscaliza\xE7\xE3o."
  _tradeOffsEn: Reviewing before publishing takes time and limits what can be opened.
    Keeping everything closed avoids the risk and blocks oversight.
  _sources:
  - Label: How a Software Engineer Deanonymized Data on 173 Million NYC Taxi Trips
      (Route Fifty, 2014)
    Url: https://www.route-fifty.com/management/2014/09/how-software-engineer-deanonymized-data-173-million-nyc-taxi-trips/93320
